
******** FILE CONTROLS ********


#### -f (Read file)

Open the specified file for reading. If this is not used, then it will
read from stdin. This command is required for auto-detection of the number
of rows of some file formats.


#### -p (Read pipe)

Open a pipe for reading, and use the specified shell command.


#### +f (Write file)

Open the specified file for writing. If this is not used, then it will
write to stdout.


#### +p (Write pipe)

Open a pipe for writing, and use the specified shell command.


******** INPUT FORMATS ********


#### -ansi (ANSI art)

S = Set to 1 to read SAUCE data, which causes some of the other parameters
to be set automatically.

b = Blank character code (default=0)

c = Initial colour (default=7)

d = Set to 1 to enable doorway mode

e = Line endings: 0=normal, 1=LF->CRLF, 2=CR->CRLF

f = Set to 1 to treat backspace and form feed as control characters. Set
to -1 to treat some control characters as graphic characters even though
they are normally not treated as graphic characters.

w = Wrapping behaviour; 0 means go to next line immediately after the
last character on the previous line, 1 means wait until another character
or a line break, 2 means never go to the next line unless an explicit line
break occurs.

v = Set to 1 to enable scrolling

x = Number of columns (default=80)

y = Number of rows (if 0 then decided automatically)


#### -artworx (Artworx Data Format)

x = Number of columns (default=80)

y = Number of rows (if 0 then decided automatically; requires seekable)


#### -bin (raw binary)

S = Set to 1 to read SAUCE data, which causes some of the other parameters
to be set automatically.

x = Number of columns (default=160)

y = Number of rows (if 0 then decided automatically; requires seekable)


#### -chr (raw PC font data)

h = Font height (if 0 then decided automatically; requires seekable)

n = Number of characters (can be 1 to 256, or 512; default=256)

o = Character code offset (default=0)


#### -ega (EGA palette)

(none)


#### -mzm (MegaZeux image file)

Only the parameter and colour are read; any other data stored in the file
will be ignored, and will not be copied into any output files.

u = Set to 1 to read the under layer instead of the main layer (this is
ignored for a layer mode MZM)


#### -vga (VGA palette)

(none)


#### -xbin (XBIN)

(none)


#### -zzt (ZZT board)

Only ZZT board files can be loaded, and not ZZT world files.

m = Set to 1 to hide the player.


******** MODIFIERS ********


#### blank (Make a new blank playfield grid)

C = Character code (default=0)

c = Colour code (default=0)

x = Width (mandatory)

y = Height (mandatory)


#### border (Border)

C = Character code (default=0; -1=thin lines, -2=thick lines)

c = Colour code (default=0)


#### cancel (Cancel)

The parameter is zero or more of the following characters:

f = Cancel font

g = Cancel grid

m = Cancel video mode

p = Cancel palette


#### color (Change colours)

A = AND mask (default=0)

X = XOR mask (default=0)


#### crop (Crop)

If any of the parameters are negative, then they are treated as counting
backward from the lower right corner. For the size, zero is considered to
be a negative number; for the offset, zero is considered to be positive.

X = X offset

Y = Y offset

x = X size

y = Y size


#### mode (Set video mode)

The parameter is zero or more of the following characters:

9 = Nine dot mode

b = Bright background (no blink)

u = Underline blue characters


#### overlay (Overlay)

Add a overlay from the grid pushed to stack to this one.

c = Colour or character code for transparency (default=0). This must be
combined with "t" to have any effect; if the colour or character (according
to that option) matches this value, then this cell will be transparent.

t = Transparency mode: 0=none, 1=colour, 2=character.

x = X offset (default=0; -1=start from right)

y = Y offset (default=0; -1=start from bottom)


#### pcpal (Load default palette)

Loads the default palette.


#### pop (Pop from stack)

Push the font, grid, and palette to the stack. Any state that already
exists will not be overridden, but any that is not defined (the "cancel"
modifier can be used to cancel them if necessary) will be restored.


#### push (Push to stack)

Push the font, grid, and palette to the stack, and then the new state will
be with none of them loaded. This is used with some other commands which
will use the data from the stack.


#### showfont (Show font)

Loads a preview of the first 256 characters of the currently selected font,
in a 16x16 arrangement.


******** OUTPUT FORMATS ********


#### +ansi (ANSI)

S = Set to 1 or 2 to apply SAUCE. If set to 2 and the e option is nonzero,
then the number of columns is one more than the actual number of columns.

d = Doorway mode: 0=disable, 1=enable implicitly, 2=enable explicitly.
If set to zero, some characters don't work, and are replaced by other
characters instead.

e = Line endings: 0=none, 1=LF, 2=CR, 3=CRLF

f = Font export: 0=none, 1=using CTerm binary format (the base64 format is
not currently implemented).

m = Set to 1 to use monochrome output mode.

s = If nonzero, then after the specified number of characters, will save
the cursor and emit CRLF and then restore the cursor. (MegaZeux does this,
allegedly due to a DOS ANSI viewer or editor using a fixed size buffer.)


#### +artworx (Artworx Data Format)

(none)


#### +bin (raw binary)

S = Set to 1 to apply SAUCE


#### +chr (raw PC font data)

(none)


#### +ega (EGA palette)

If the palette is not already EGA format, it is converted.


#### +farbfeld (Farbfeld)

Renders the picture as farbfeld. The font, palette, and grid must all be
already loaded, in order for this to work, otherwise it is an error.

Blinking is not implemented; if blinking is enabled then any blinking
characters will be displayed as solid on, without a bright background.


#### +info (Show information)

Displays some information about the currently loaded data.


#### +mzm (MegaZeux image file)

This always writes a layer mode MZM2 file.


#### +vga (VGA palette)

If the palette is not already VGA format, it is converted.


#### +xbin (XBIN)

c = Set to 1 to enable compression.

